From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:29:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: twl4030: keep feeding a watchdog that cannot be
 stopped

On some TWL5031s, as in the Nokia N950 and N9, the watchdog keeps
running after 0 is written to WATCHDOG_CFG; Nokia's 2.6.32 kernel checks
for this at boot ("HACK: TWL5031 WDT can't be disabled. Automatic WDT
refresh started", logged on every boot of the N950 at hand) and kicks it
from a timer. Mainline writes 0 at probe and leaves it alone, so the
phone resets at most 30 s after the boot loader last kicked it, unless
user space opens the watchdog in time.

Read the register back after stopping. If it still runs, re-arm it with
the full timeout and mark it WDOG_HW_RUNNING, so that the watchdog core
keeps it fed until user space opens it, and again after user space
closes it.

Untested on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/watchdog/twl4030_wdt.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/twl4030_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/twl4030_wdt.c
index 8c80d0481..cb0c77276 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/twl4030_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/twl4030_wdt.c
@@ -34,7 +34,29 @@ static int twl4030_wdt_start(struct watchdog_device *wdt)
 
 static int twl4030_wdt_stop(struct watchdog_device *wdt)
 {
-	return twl4030_wdt_write(0);
+	u8 left;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = twl4030_wdt_write(0);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Some TWL5031s (Nokia N950 and N9) are configured so that their
+	 * watchdog keeps running whatever is written here; Nokia's kernel
+	 * kicked it from a timer ("TWL5031 WDT can't be disabled"). Re-arm
+	 * it with the full timeout and let the watchdog core keep it fed
+	 * until user space opens it, instead of a reset 30 s later.
+	 */
+	ret = twl_i2c_read_u8(TWL_MODULE_PM_RECEIVER, &left,
+			      TWL4030_WATCHDOG_CFG_REG_OFFS);
+	if (ret || !left)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (!test_and_set_bit(WDOG_HW_RUNNING, &wdt->status))
+		dev_info(wdt->parent, "cannot be stopped, kept running\n");
+
+	return twl4030_wdt_start(wdt);
 }
 
 static int twl4030_wdt_set_timeout(struct watchdog_device *wdt,
-- 
2.56.0

